flowchart TB
    accTitle: Brook event flow
    accDescr: One shared execution model carries graph-node deliveries, optional agent work, correlated origin results and authorized sink effects. Logical routing can bypass agents.
    ingress["Ingress<br/>Producer + durable admission"]
    processors["Processors / routing Operator<br/>Configured paths and transforms"]
    agent["Agent node<br/>AgentConfig + swappable harness"]
    work["Durable asynchronous work<br/>Await-result correlation"]
    reply["Authenticated reply<br/>Accepted outcome + origin delivery"]
    resume["Fresh origin invocation<br/>Current context + exact evidence"]
    sink["Authorized sink intent<br/>Applied / not applied / unknown"]
    ingress --> processors
    processors -->|selected path| agent
    processors -->|direct sink path| sink
    agent --> work
    work --> reply
    reply -->|stored origin binding| resume
    resume --> sink
